Stage 1: 
Role & Objective
You are an Expert Principal Full-Stack Engineer. Your task is to build a high-quality, fully functional Single-Page Application (SPA) prototype for a Smart India Hackathon (SIH) project. The platform is a Centralized Academia–Industry Collaboration & Skill Mapping Portal.
Tech Stack & Constraints
⚬	Strictly Vanilla: HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript only. No React, no Tailwind, no external frameworks, no backend server.
⚬	State Management: Use browser localStorage to simulate a database.
⚬	File Structure: Exactly 5 files: index.html, style.css, backend.js, auth.js, and app.js.
⚬	UI/UX Theme: Clean, neat, professional, non-flashy (slate/light color palette). Take layout inspiration from Skill India Digital.
Core Requirements
1. Authentication & Onboarding (auth.js & UI)
⚬	Dynamic registration with 3 Roles: Student, Institute/Faculty, and Industry.
⚬	Student/Faculty Shared Inputs: First/Middle/Last Name, Contact, Email, Password, Confirm Password, State, City/District, Gender, Last passed course, Aadhaar Number (Keep mock data as generic placeholders, no real digits), Upload ID Card placeholder. Dropdown to select College/Institute (Hardcode 5 dummy institutes).
⚬	Student Specific: Student ID, Academic Percentage.
⚬	Faculty Specific: Faculty ID, Registration Number.
⚬	Industry Inputs: Company Name, Business Email, Corporate ID (CIN/GST), Industry Sector, Password.
2. Profile Setup Module
⚬	Photo upload placeholder.
⚬	Skills: Multi-select array of at least 50 skills (e.g., C++, Java, Python, MySQL, HTML/CSS, Accounting, Blockchain, Cybersecurity, Digital Marketing, Excel). Multi-select for "Skills to Learn".
⚬	Upload previous qualifications/degrees.
⚬	Student: Select Branch/Department, Current Year, Date of Birth (must be disabled/non-editable after setup).
⚬	Faculty: Select Department, Toggle for "Are you TPO?" (If Yes, show TPO ID input).
3. Student Dashboard (Sidebar Navigation in app.js & index.html)
⚬	Dashboard: Show courses joined, visual completion % (CSS progress bars), verified vs. unverified skills badges, and a GitHub-style activity contribution heatmap.
⚬	Programmes & Events: List nearby localized education workshops, seminars, and industry expert talks.
⚬	Learn & Upskill: Grid of 10 core course cards (Python, Java, C++, MySQL, HTML/CSS, Accounting, Blockchain, Cybersecurity, Digital Marketing, Excel). Cards must show Description, Duration, Rating, Level (Beginner/Intermediate/Expert), and Provider.
⚬	Assessment: W3Schools-style UI for skill verification. Include a mock 10-question test layout for a selected skill.
⚬	Articles: LinkedIn-style feed for announcements and news from institutes/companies.
⚬	Help: FAQ section and direct links to government education portals.
4. Data Layer (backend.js)
⚬	Create robust mock data structures. Pre-load 5 institutes, the 50+ skills array, 10 upskilling courses, 5 local events, and sample articles. Do not generate real government ID digits in the mock data.
Execution Instructions (Crucial for Token Limits)
Do NOT generate all 5 files at once, as you will hit your output token limit. Follow this exact sequence:
⚬	Step 1: Acknowledge this prompt and generate ONLY the full, complete code for index.html and style.css.
⚬	At the end of your response, ask me to reply with "Next" to provide backend.js and auth.js.
⚬	Wait for my prompt to generate the remaining files.
Execute Step 1 now.

